# ================ ROW 6 (Critic L-4): where seed 1207954461's 258 fires come from ==========================
# Asked for as a diagnosis and produced by reading that run's own sim.log rather than by reasoning about it.
# Source: /proj_soc/user_dev/fzhang/ibex_dv_out/regress_chkfix/runs/gen_test_irq_basic_1207954461/sim.log,
# runtime-2's re-run at 9c7f8f6 (265755454 bytes). Script: <scratch>/l54/diag258.py, one pass, every figure
# re-derived here and none adopted.
#   693238 real UVM_ERROR lines. By id, with the first timestamp each appears (UVM log ticks, 10 ps):
#     450021 sva_ibus_outstanding_max     first@26503500
#      70208 sva_rvalid_legal             first@15158500
#      70208 sva_ibus_rvalid_outstanding  first@15158500
#      23387 isa_insn                     first@ 9290500
#      23384 isa_pc                       first@ 9300500
#      23369 crash_dump                   first@ 9499500
#      18553 isa_pc_next                  first@ 9290500
#       9126 isa_rd                       first@ 9326500
#        258 irq_entry                    first@15737500
#          3 sva_rvfi_irq_valid_exclusive first@ 6591500
#          1 sva_ibus_gnt_only_with_req   first@ 9250500
#   258 fires, 18 distinct raised bitmaps, mstatus 00000088 at all 258, mie 7fff0888 at all 258, raise-to-fire
#   order deltas 18:153 19:67 20:23 21:7 22:3 23:5. Those five figures reproduce runtime-2's record exactly.
# THE DIAGNOSIS IS THE ORDERING. The first instruction-level divergence between model and DUT is at 9290500,
# SIX THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND FORTY-SEVEN CYCLES BEFORE the first irq_entry fire at 15737500, and 23387
# isa_insn mismatches have already been reported by then. The core is executing 0x00000000 at pc 0x80000022
# while the model is at 0x80000154 ("Illegal instruction (hart 0) at PC 0x80000022: 0x00000000"; pc 80000022
# appears on 9084 lines). The bus anomaly precedes even that: sva_ibus_gnt_only_with_req fires once at
# 9250500, forty cycles before the divergence.
# So the fires are DOWNSTREAM of a fetch and execution breakdown, not the masked-window mechanism. And they
# are the checker telling the truth: at every one of the 258, mstatus has MIE set and the raised line's enable
# bit is set, so the interrupt was takeable and a core that was still running its program would have taken it.
# This seed is not a checker defect, it is not fixed by this landing, and it must not be counted against it.
# ONE CORRECTION TO THE CRITIC'S FILE, whose bytes I do not touch. Its Section 3 says rtl-arch's ibus-signature
# table "names 1207954461 with the same firing counts". It does not: rtl-arch's table in
# gen_ibus_props_irq_signature_reading.md:51-54 gives that seed sva_ibus_rvalid_outstanding 70199 and
# sva_ibus_outstanding_max 449948, where this run has 70208 and 450021. The two are different runs of the same
# seed, at 4017573 and at 9c7f8f6. The attribution is right and rests on the signature and the ordering, not
# on equal numbers, and every number the Critic states for THIS run I reproduce exactly.
# ONE CORRECTION TO runtime-2's RECORD. gen_chkfix_reruns.yaml:17 says the deciding property "fires 6 times".
# It fires 3. Six lines mention the id: each firing emits a VCS assertion-source line and a UVM_ERROR line.
# The same tally-shaped error as the 343-against-334 count, in a different disguise.
#
